    "reason": "The only upstream evidence is the v2.0.0 CRD file for protection.crossplane.io_usages.yaml [ev-147c26b74d68] (excerpt \"---\"), which shows a CRD was added but says nothing about anything failing or needing migration. The line \"Install or update CRDs before upgrading if you manage them separately\" is a generic note from the computed diff, not an upstream statement. So migration-required (action-required, high) has no support and would over-claim mandatory work. We would need release notes or an upgrade guide saying whether Crossplane fails without this CRD before choosing a kind; until then, \"none\" isn't proven either.",
